- op: discuss  # 9a51
  at: '2026-09-30T11:08:08Z'  # 9a51
  by: agent  # 9a51
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9a51
  clock: 5  # 9a51
  nonce: 9a51  # 9a51
  message: "REOPENED 2026-09-30 with a positive counterexample: the statement is general (every repository walk terminates) and the #1328 fix covered the filed instance only. Re-running arti's WI-dikit arms on dev 554aa88b8b (with #1328) hung again, 37 min at ~705 MB; faulthandler stack: pathlib.is_dir <- hypergumbo_lang_mainstream.py._detect_source_roots (py.py:2412) <- analyze_python. The same hand-written iterdir() stack walk, pushing every entry.is_dir(), exists in py.py _detect_source_roots and py_deps.py (pyproject walk, :252) as well. Sweep: 39 .iterdir() call sites across packages; the three unbounded repository walks are supply_chain (fixed), py.py and py_deps.py; os.walk (discovery, cli) defaults to followlinks=False; the rest are single-level listings or non-repository directories. Fix: one shared predicate in core for whether a repository walk may descend into an entry, used by all three."  # 9a51
