- op: discuss  # 1d22
  at: '2026-09-30T12:39:39Z'  # 1d22
  by: agent  # 1d22
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1d22
  clock: 7  # 1d22
  nonce: 1d22  # 1d22
  message: "Fixed across the family in PR #1331 (merged, dev ad028b5042), after #1328 fixed the first two walks. discovery.walks_into(entry, skip) is the one rule every hand-written repository walk asks: a real directory, not skipped, not dot-prefixed, never a symlink (what os.walk and Path.rglob already do); supply_chain's manifest walks, py._detect_source_roots and py_deps._find_pyproject_files all route through it. Sweep: 39 .iterdir() sites -- those were the unbounded repository walks; os.walk defaults to followlinks=False; the rest are single-level. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the filed repro on merged dev: hypergumbo verify-claims on arti (maint/rust-maint-common/{maint,common} -> .) completes in 122 s, rc 1, 9 verdicts (was killed after 30+ min twice). Tests: alarm-guarded cycle tests for all four walkers; a type-clean mutation of the predicate reds the Python ones with TimeoutError. The general statement is asserted for the hand-written iterdir() walks the sweep found; a future walker is covered only if it asks walks_into."  # 1d22
